<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">growth</ansi>

Companions grow on their own. Levels give a companion stat points
(1 every 2 levels, as the world ships), and their archetype decides where the
points go. You never spend a companion's stat points, and they never pile up
unspent. Levels also give training points, which you do spend, on optional
skills such as Cooking (<ansi fg="command">help company train</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How the points are dealt</ansi>

Each archetype leans toward the stats it needs, by these weights out of 10:

  Warrior   strength 4, vitality 3, speed 2, perception 1
  Rogue     speed 4, perception 3, strength 2, smarts 1
  Wizard    mysticism 4, smarts 3, perception 2, speed 1
  Witch     mysticism 4, smarts 3, perception 2, vitality 1
  Cleric    mysticism 3, vitality 3, smarts 2, strength 2
  Ranger    perception 4, speed 3, strength 2, vitality 1

Points go round the stats in that proportion: of every 10 points, a
warrior puts 4 in strength, 3 in vitality, 2 in speed, and 1 in
perception. A companion without an archetype spreads them evenly
(<ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>).

A companion's points always come from their level alone. A level lost
when they are raised from the dead can take its point back, and earning that
level again gives the same point again, never an extra one. Automatic racial
stats grow smoothly each level (<ansi fg="command">help progression</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">A focus</ansi>

You may give each companion one focus stat. It adds 2 to that stat's
weight, so a warrior with a vitality focus deals strength 4, vitality 5,
speed 2, perception 1. The focus changes how all of their points are
dealt, at once, and costs nothing; you can change it whenever you aren't
in a battle. Health and mana never rise from a change, though a lower
maximum lowers them to fit.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">company growth</ansi>
  Each companion's archetype, level, focus, weights, and the points
  their level has dealt so far.

  <ansi fg="command">company growth [member] [stat]</ansi>
  Give a companion a focus: strength, speed, smarts, vitality,
  mysticism, or perception (the first letters will do, e.g. vit).

  <ansi fg="command">company growth [member] balanced</ansi>
  Clear the focus: they grow by their archetype alone.

Your own stats are yours to train (<ansi fg="command">help stat-train</ansi>).
Companions earn experience from battles and from contracts
(<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help contracts</ansi>).
